 {"status":"complete","id":"LORE-071","created_at":"2026-11-16T03:45:23.757136Z","title":"Scheduled re-validation is now armed (weekly user timer) — absorb/refresh loop needs the DuckBrain adapter next","detail":{"fingerprint":"6c78d93d7489531f36801fb3d4a599e5235c69d4bfd796e0b3e3f29d49de21e4","evidence":[{"run_id":"e7900e43","ts":"2026-11-16T13:49:46.200516Z"}]},"priority":"P2","source":null,"reasoning":"LIVE OPERATION 2026-11-11 (evidence /tmp/lore-review-20261111/): lore had NO freshness automation at all (grep-verified: no cron/systemd/watch; absorb is manual, proposal-only). Deployed lore-validate.timer (user systemd): weekly Monday 07:30, runs lore validate --execute from /home/kara/get-h3/lore (CWD-relative board read), logs to /home/kara/.local/share/lore/weekly-validate.log. First live run already shows the coupling: the gateway-drain-window gate's logsey query fails on stale-index fallback (logsey index is now under a live watcher — see LOGSEY-111). NEXT (this row): absorb still has no automatic trigger. The strongest candidate per the trigger analysis: board events.jsonl appends with structured class_id/incident closures — a watcher normalizing those into absorb trails, proposal-only. Also map Auger's DuckBrain decision-table writes (D-*/verdict/unknown/break/assumption rows, deterministic markdown export, auger HEAD 6616a25) into lore EvidenceBlocks via adapter — Auger is the write format, NOT a trigger. ACCEPTANCE: (1) weekly validate run lands in the log with per-class outcomes; (2) absorb consumes at least one machine-generated trail (board-event-derived or Auger-derived) end-to-end as a proposal; (3) no runbook is modified without operator approval (existing absorb contract preserved).","review_notes":null,"ts":null,"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-16T13:49:46.200516Z","acceptance_criteria":"DELIVERABLES: (1) A board-event trigger: a read-only watcher that reads the local coding-hermes boards' events.jsonl files, normalizes new task_completed / class-carrying events into lore EvidenceBlocks (proposal-only input), with a persisted per-board cursor (file offset) so a restart never re-reads already-seen events. (2) An Auger adapter: reads Auger's DuckBrain decision-table exports (D-* rows: verdict / unknown / break / assumption; the deterministic markdown export format) and maps each row to an EvidenceBlock with explicit provenance (source=auger, table, row id). (3) End-to-end wiring: the absorb path consumes at least one machine-generated trail (board-event-derived or Auger-derived) and emits an absorb PROPOSAL through the existing absorb_proposal/absorb_sweep contract — nothing writes a runbook without operator approval. (4) A docs page under docs/ linked from the README docs table; no production trigger service is enabled in this row (installation stays a documented, owner-run step). TESTS: worker creates the new test files; prove them by whole-package runs: uv run pytest tests/ -q (plus uv run ruff check lore/). Both-ways falsifiers, quoted in the report: (a) the cursor-resume test FAILS once with cursor persistence stubbed to memory-only, then passes restored; (b) the proposal-only guard test FAILS if the trigger path writes a runbook directly instead of only proposing. Use fixtures under tests/fixtures/ (copies of real board events.jsonl and a real Auger markdown export) — never read or write live board files from tests. ACCEPTANCE: (1) Appending a new synthetic event to a fixture board and re-running the trigger yields EvidenceBlocks for exactly the new events; a second run with the persisted cursor yields zero duplicates. (2) The Auger fixture maps to EvidenceBlocks whose provenance names table and row id. (3) One machine-generated trail flows end-to-end into an absorb PROPOSAL, and the run asserts no file under the runbook tree changed. (4) uv run lore validate (or the repo's validate entrypoint as documented) still exits 0 on the repo's own dogfood corpus. EVIDENCE: the closing report quotes the named test list with wall times, both falsifier outputs, one sample EvidenceBlock with provenance, one sample absorb proposal, and the validate exit code.","worker_status":"in_progress","foreman_note":"Claimed by LOGSEY-loop coordinator cron 2026-11-16; worktree /home/kara/get-h3/lore-wt-LORE-071, branch lore-071-absorb-trigger; criteria expanded from reasoning (gate was FAIL:empty).","commit_hash":"0e662b1d7d8d6e04dea746582fea2342d1fecfcf","worker_summary":"CLOSED. Board-event trigger (lore/trigger.py: read-only JSONL watcher, atomic persisted byte-offset cursor, refuses replay past EOF) + Auger DuckBrain adapter (provenance source=auger:<table>:<row_id>) feeding absorb_sweep as PROPOSAL-ONLY. Worker f264edc (gpt-6.1-terra, deleg_d7c3c5e7); coordinator follow-up 0e662b1 fixed the vacuous falsifier (dead monkeypatch -> direct memory-only-store injection) flagged by the tier-2 judge. Evidence: uv run pytest tests/ -q = 572 passed; tier-2 judge PASS (run e7900e43, verdict 56e9ac44: no-runbook-write proven by grep + test, cursor failure paths raise instead of replaying, live restart replays nothing). Residual: no production timer/service installed for the trigger — installation is a documented owner-run step (docs/ABSORB-TRIGGER.md); proposal-only contract preserved.","completed_at":"2026-11-16T09:10:00-05:00"}
 {"status":"complete","id":"QA-LORE-5","created_at":"2026-11-16T23:55:05.001125Z","title":"[P3] chaos-corruption cell can never grade lore: DB-only candidate set while durable state is .lore/validate-history.jsonl — ship .qa/chaos-probes/corruption.sh","detail":{"metadata":{"source":"qa-foreman"},"fingerprint":"d16b4d360cb83ce4f36b5bc76261201ef16f7328473342815bb7f74694e42c84","evidence":[{"run_id":"lore-qa-2026-11-16-23-09-49","ts":"2026-11-16T23:55:05.001125Z","tree_fp":"12673b7db722498ee40a3ce21505684f3520a1827bf08cbb21d70c2624642399","artifacts":["/home/kara/.hermes/qa/harvest/lore-qa-2026-11-16-23-09-49/cells.txt"]},{"run_id":"736e959b","ts":"2026-11-17T05:45:31.169614Z","tree_fp":"fa875ed71871dd9799c2b382d35e685154e8f5e8694690446cef4f1fee4a0bb0","artifacts":["docs/qa/evidence/run-QA-LORE-5/README.md"]}]},"priority":"P3","source":null,"reasoning":"QA lane lore-qa clean-machine JIT battery 2026-11-16 (bunker-mvp agent 5934878a, tested tree e5517a0): chaos-corruption graded N/A \"no db/state files in repo\" because bunker-qa.sh builds its candidate set from *.db/*.sqlite/*.sqlite3 only, while lore persists validation history as JSONL. Harness limitation, remedy owned by the repo via the documented .qa/chaos-probes escape hatch.","review_notes":null,"ts":null,"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-17T05:46:16.377695Z","acceptance_criteria":"Add .qa/chaos-probes/corruption.sh (executable, self-contained, offline, <=60s) that exercises lore's real torn-state read path and self-grades with the harness contract:\n\n1. In a throwaway temp dir (never the repo tree), create .lore/validate-history.jsonl with several well-formed JSONL records, then truncate the file mid-line and append one non-JSON garbage line.\n2. Exercise the product read path on that state: `lore consult` (lore/__main__.py) and the history reader behind it must not raise, must skip the malformed line, and must still report the well-formed records rather than \"never validated\".\n3. Second rung: make .lor