 {"id":"RELEASE-LORE-008","title":"[P3] deployed CLI lags the release — host uv tool get-h3-lore reports 0.1.2 while v0.2.0 is published, and the install floats on the default branch","status":"complete","priority":"P3","created_by":"releng-lane lore-releng-2026-11-16-23-09-49","reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-17T00:16Z during the re-fire sweep of tick lore-releng-2026-11-16-23-09-49. The release layers are all correct (tag v0.2.0 -> 165cc8f, release published, tag-gated release-check green), but the copy a user actually runs does not carry it: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/get-h3-lore/lib/python3.14/site-packages reports Version: 0.1.2 (get_h3_lore-0.1.2.dist-info, lore/__init__.py '__version__ = 0.1.2'). The uv receipt pins no ref (requirements = [{name = 'get-h3-lore', git = 'https://github.com/get-h3/lore'}]), so the host install tracks whatever the default branch was at install time — it can be both stale and unreproducible. Not a release defect; a deployed-surface drift. Readiness gate for contrast: scripts/release.sh --dry-run at tip 7788fb4 reports clean tree, CI success on HEAD sha, version 0.2.0 -> tag v0.2.0, and refuses only because the tag already exists.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"3cb7b2f452ed9390eda4b65767b45d7c9ecbfad5a102b869baa3d5d488d80e32","evidence":[{"run_id":"03752b22","ts":"2026-11-17T05:20:40+00:00","tree_fp":"956ccb9c39348562a087cb00b12a9ee4f5cc3b4dfd1a9e78a2e21abea622817b","artifacts":["docs/qa/evidence/run-RELEASE-LORE-008/README.md"]}]},"source":"releng-lane sweep 2026-11-16","acceptance_criteria":["On the host, the installed distribution reports Version: 0.2.0 — get_h3_lore-0.2.0.dist-info/METADATA and lore/__init__.py __version__ both read 0.2.0 — and `command -v lore` resolves to that uv tool install.","The installed CLI is exercised live after the upgrade (a lore subcommand runs with exit 0) rather than inferred from metadata alone.","The install names the released tag instead of floating on the default branch, and the exact inst