 {"id": "DOC-11", "title": "P4 — five doc sites say no weekly lint schedule exists while lore-validate.timer re-validates the checkout every Monday", "status": "pending", "priority": "P4", "created_by": null, "reasoning": "DOC ROT, measured 2026-11-16 at origin/main 7788fb4. Doc severity is P4 by Bane ruling 2026-09-30 (documentation findings never outrank functional defects); P4 is this row being filed, NOT a new assessment of severity.\n\nCLAIM IN DOCS (five sites, one absolute statement)\n- README.md:409-410 — \"No schedule is installed yet (a separate task owns the weekly timer).\"\n- README.md:489-490 — \"Still planned: runbook-store materialization and the scheduled weekly lint.\"\n- docs/INSTALL.md:150-153 — \"...the weekly *schedule* that would run it for you is not installed (that is a separate task).\"\n- docs/INSTALL.md:441-443 — \"No scheduled lint / re-validation yet. ... nothing runs on a schedule.\"\n- docs/RUNBOOK-STORE.md:132 — \"nothing runs the lint on a timer today, so re-validation happens only ...\"\n\nREALITY (commands run, outputs pasted)\n$ systemctl --user list-timers --all | grep -i lore\nMon 2026-11-23 07:30:00 -05   6 days Mon 2026-11-16 07:30:00 -05   12h ago lore-validate.timer   lore-validate.service\n$ cat /home/kara/.config/systemd/user/lore-validate.timer\n[Timer] OnCalendar=Mon *-*-* 07:30:00 / Persistent=true ; [Install] WantedBy=timers.target\n$ cat /home/kara/.config/systemd/user/lore-validate.service\nExecStart=/home/kara/.local/bin/lore validate --execute --format md ; WorkingDirectory=/home/kara/get-h3/lore ; StandardOutput=append:/home/kara/.local/share/lore/weekly-validate.log\n$ wc -l /home/kara/.local/share/lore/weekly-validate.log -> 138 lines; tail shows the 2026-11-16 07:30 run ending \"history: 13 record(s) appended to .lore/validate-history.jsonl (local lint history, not operator attestation)\"\n\nSCOPE / HONESTY: the timer is operator-armed OUT of the repo (user units in ~/.config/systemd/user, dated 2026-11-15); the 0.2.0 release ships no installer or service (CHANGELOG.md:25 \"no production timer or service is installed by this release\"). The defect is the absolute wording — the docs tell an operator that re-validation never happens, while this project checkout has been re-validated weekly and the lint history is accumulating in .lore/validate-history.jsonl.\n\nMarker: ch:trace row=DOC-11 spec=docs/RUNBOOK-STORE.md witness=live:systemctl --user lore-validate.timer doc=README.md evidence=/home/kara/.local/share/lore/weekly-validate.log", "detail": {"fingerprint": "e3e8452a2795c7ea25e128145861619e4dfe685a0a95b3069886a1721c7636a8"}, "source": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1) Each of the five sites named above stops asserting that no schedule exists. 2) The docs state, in one short paragraph (README Status + INSTALL \"What this tool is NOT\"): a weekly user-systemd timer CAN be armed by the operator (this fleet runs one: OnCalendar=Mon *-*-* 07:30:00, Persistent=true, unit files ~/.config/systemd/user/lore-validate.timer and lore-validate.service, executing \"lore validate --execute --format md\" from the checkout, output appended to ~/.local/share/lore/weekly-validate.log). 3) The same paragraph keeps the release scope honest: the package itself installs no timer or service, so a fresh source install has none until the operator arms it. 4) Verification for the close-out: paste systemctl --user list-timers --all | grep -i lore, the two unit files, wc -l of the log, and re-grep the five sites to show no absolute \"nothing runs on a schedule\" wording survives.", "capability_tags": ["docs", "runbook-store", "operations"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-17T00:38:32+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-17T00:38:32+00:00", "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "completed_at": null}
